# Generated structural ontology index (main#939 child rollout deploy#571, #820 C×T2).
# The structural layer is "always-current-by-regeneration" (#857) — regenerated
# wholesale from source by the owned generator (ontology_gen in noorinalabs-main,
# via `python3 scripts/structural_ontology.py emit`, which merges the auto-derived
# Python graph with this repo's hand-curated HCL/YAML stub). Committing it made
# EVERY concurrent PR that touched any source file conflict on a whole-file
# generated artifact that carries no information (the only correct resolution is
# "discard both, regenerate"), and GitHub's server-side merge cannot run the
# per-clone union merge-driver that tried to paper over it. So it is no longer
# committed: it is a build product, produced on demand and read locally.
# noorinalabs-main's cross-repo aggregator (ontology_gen.aggregate) regenerates
# this repo's index locally before rolling up, so nothing depends on a committed
# copy. See issue deploy#571 / main#939.
ontology/structural/

# Agent scratch space — commit-message drafts and working files. Gitignored in the
# parent org repo; this repo had drifted, and a draft reached a branch bound for main
# (deploy#574 review). Never a build input.
.claude/scratch/
